# PR #1297 review comment — cdz-kernel/src/kernel.rs (v-agent-harness)

Mirrored from https://github.com/camshaft/cadenza/pull/1297 (PR: "cand: v-agent-harness — 8291be808").

## `fork_for_query` duplicates `Session::genesis` construction (Copilot, kernel.rs:218) — maintainability
> `fork_for_query` duplicates `Session::genesis` construction logic (field initialization + pushing a
> Genesis event). This makes it easy for the fork behavior to drift if `Session` gains new fields or
> `genesis()` changes its invariants. Prefer delegating to `Session::genesis(self.reducer_hash())`
> and then overriding only the fields that must differ (KV clone + `last_now`).

Delegate to `Session::genesis(...)` then override only the deltas (KV clone + `last_now`), so a new
`Session` field or a `genesis()` invariant change can't silently desync the fork path.
